---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StaticSiteHeader from "@/components/StaticSiteHeader.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methodology | gpaestimate.com"
  description="How gpaestimate.com calculates GPA, where grading-scale data comes from, and what our numbers do and don't guarantee."
>
  <StaticSiteHeader currentPath="/methodology" />
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "GPA Calculator", href: "/" }, { label: "Methodology" }]} />
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-graphite sm:text-4xl">Methodology</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-graphite-muted">Last reviewed: August 2026</p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-graphite-muted">
      This page explains exactly how gpaestimate.com calculates the numbers it shows you, and
      what those numbers do and don't tell you.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-graphite">The calculation</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-graphite-muted">
      For every course, we multiply its grade-point value by its credit hours to get quality
      points. We sum quality points across all valid rows and divide by total attempted credits.
      No rounding happens until the final GPA, credit total, and quality-point total are
      displayed, each to two decimal places.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-graphite">Grading scales</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-graphite-muted">
      The grade-point values behind each scale are configuration data, not hardcoded logic — this
      is what lets us add more institutional scales over time. The "Standard 4.0" scale reflects
      the plus/minus convention used by most U.S. colleges. University-specific grading
      information should always be confirmed against official institutional sources, since
      schools set their own policies and can change them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-graphite">What our numbers are — and aren't</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-graphite-muted">
      <li>Results are estimates. Verify anything that matters against your official transcript.</li>
      <li>
        Standing labels like "Typical Dean's List range" describe common patterns, not your
        school's actual policy — Dean's List, honors, and probation thresholds vary by
        institution.
      </li>
      <li>
        The GPA Predictor solves a simple algebraic target; it doesn't know your school's specific
        rules about repeated courses, grade replacement, or rounding.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-graphite">Your data</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-graphite-muted">
      Calculator data remains on your device unless you explicitly choose to save a semester,
      which stores it in your browser's local storage only. Nothing is sent to a server.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-graphite-soft">
      This page is educational information, not academic, financial, or admissions advice.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
